    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0279" n="245" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg245"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr.
                            Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-09-01"><hi rendition="#italic">September 1, 1897</hi></date>.
                        (Received September 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 82.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence, and
                    in particular to Mr. Uhl’s dispatch No. 296, of March 15 last, I have the honor
                    to transmit herewith a copy, with translation, of a note which has to-day been
                    received from the German foreign office in regard to the freight charges upon
                    woods of American origin on railroads under Government control. A copy of this
                    note has been sent to Mr. Carl Gartner, of Hamburg, upon whose complaint the
                    original action in this matter was taken by the embassy.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Andrew D. White.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d219-a1.xml" xpointer="d219-a1"/>
            </div>
